{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_rY7gyOPYv8wJchKGs2NVPrwO","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tlayout: layouts/base.vto\n3\ttitle: NetScript — durable, typed applications on Deno\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t{{ comp.hero({\n7\t  tagline: \"Your checkout survives the crash. Your types survive the refactor.\",\n8\t  subhead: \"NetScript is a framework for durable, typed, full-stack applications on Deno.\",\n9\t  ctas: [\n10\t    { label: \"Start a workspace\", href: \"/quickstart/\", primary: true }\n11\t  ]\n12\t}) }}\n13\t\n14\t{{ comp.featureGrid({ items: [\n15\t  {\n16\t    title: \"Durability is a state machine\",\n17\t    body: \"Define state transitions and compensation in TypeScript; the runtime records every step through its saga store instead of treating a multi-step flow as a retry loop.\",\n18\t    href: \"/durable-workflows/\"\n19\t  },\n20\t  {\n21\t    title: \"One contract crosses the stack\",\n22\t    body: \"Write one oRPC contract to power your service handlers, drive the OpenAPI document, and type the SDK calls your Fresh page loaders make.\",\n23\t    href: \"/services-sdk/\"\n24\t  },\n25\t  {\n26\t    title: \"One command starts the traced fleet\",\n27\t    body: \"aspire start brings up the whole generated resource graph; the dashboard then reports resource health and carries logs and traces across it.\",\n28\t    href: \"/observability/\"\n29\t  }\n30\t] }) }}\n31\t\n32\t{{ comp.tabbedCode({ tabs: [\n33\t  {\n34\t    label: \"A checkout with a real refund path\",\n35\t    lang: \"ts\",\n36\t    code: \"import { defineSaga, sagaCompensate, send } from '@netscript/plugin-sagas-core';\\nimport type { SagaCorrelationKey } from '@netscript/plugin-sagas-core';\\n\\ntype Checkout = { status: 'pending' | 'paid' };\\ntype Failure = { orderId: string; reason: string };\\ntype CheckoutEvent =\\n  | { type: 'payment.captured'; payload: { orderId: string } }\\n  | { type: 'inventory.failed'; payload: Failure };\\n\\nconst checkout = defineSaga('checkout')\\n  .state<Checkout>({ status: 'pending' })\\n  .correlate<CheckoutEvent>((event) => event.payload.orderId as SagaCorrelationKey)\\n  .on<'payment.captured', { orderId: string }>(\\n    'payment.captured',\\n    (saga, event) => {\\n      saga.state.status = 'paid';\\n      return [send('inventory.reserve', { orderId: event.payload.orderId })];\\n    },\\n  )\\n  .on<'inventory.failed', Failure>('inventory.failed', (_saga, event) => [\\n    sagaCompensate(\\n      { type: 'payment.captured', payload: { orderId: event.payload.orderId } },\\n      event.payload.reason,\\n    ),\\n  ])\\n  .compensate<'payment.captured', { orderId: string }>(\\n    'payment.captured',\\n    (_saga, event) => [send('payment.refund', { orderId: event.payload.orderId })],\\n  )\\n  .build();\"\n37\t  }\n38\t] }) }}\n39\t\n40\t<p class=\"ns-lede\">\n41\tThe definition correlates both events by <code>orderId</code>. When <code>inventory.failed</code>\n42\tarrives, its handler returns a compensation request for <code>payment.captured</code>. Executing that\n43\trequest needs a saga bus bridge with a compensator; surviving a restart needs a durable store. With\n44\tthat wiring, the registered handler emits <code>payment.refund</code>.\n45\t<a href=\"{{ '/durable-workflows/' |> url }}\">See the durability model</a>.\n46\t</p>\n47\t\n48\t<nav class=\"ns-cluster\" aria-label=\"Choose the next page\">\n49\t  <a href=\"{{ '/quickstart/' |> url }}\">Run it</a> ·\n50\t  <a href=\"{{ '/concepts/' |> url }}\">Understand it</a> ·\n51\t  <a href=\"{{ '/why/' |> url }}\">Decide whether it fits</a>\n52\t</nav>\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a83c9845-4a4d-49af-b9fe-4d6db86478d5","uuid":"714823e5-52dd-4f0e-9a7a-054c44704bfc","timestamp":"2026-08-04T10:25:06.380Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/index.vto","content":"---\nlayout: layouts/base.vto\ntitle: NetScript — durable, typed applications on Deno\n---\n\n{{ comp.hero({\n  tagline: \"Your checkout survives the crash. Your types survive the refactor.\",\n  subhead: \"NetScript is a framework for durable, typed, full-stack applications on Deno.\",\n  ctas: [\n    { label: \"Start a workspace\", href: \"/quickstart/\", primary: true }\n  ]\n}) }}\n\n{{ comp.featureGrid({ items: [\n  {\n    title: \"Durability is a state machine\",\n    body: \"Define state transitions and compensation in TypeScript; the runtime records every step through its saga store instead of treating a multi-step flow as a retry loop.\",\n    href: \"/durable-workflows/\"\n  },\n  {\n    title: \"One contract crosses the stack\",\n    body: \"Write one oRPC contract to power your service handlers, drive the OpenAPI document, and type the SDK calls your Fresh page loaders make.\",\n    href: \"/services-sdk/\"\n  },\n  {\n    title: \"One command starts the traced fleet\",\n    body: \"aspire start brings up the whole generated resource graph; the dashboard then reports resource health and carries logs and traces across it.\",\n    href: \"/observability/\"\n  }\n] }) }}\n\n{{ comp.tabbedCode({ tabs: [\n  {\n    label: \"A checkout with a real refund path\",\n    lang: \"ts\",\n    code: \"import { defineSaga, sagaCompensate, send } from '@netscript/plugin-sagas-core';\\nimport type { SagaCorrelationKey } from '@netscript/plugin-sagas-core';\\n\\ntype Checkout = { status: 'pending' | 'paid' };\\ntype Failure = { orderId: string; reason: string };\\ntype CheckoutEvent =\\n  | { type: 'payment.captured'; payload: { orderId: string } }\\n  | { type: 'inventory.failed'; payload: Failure };\\n\\nconst checkout = defineSaga('checkout')\\n  .state<Checkout>({ status: 'pending' })\\n  .correlate<CheckoutEvent>((event) => event.payload.orderId as SagaCorrelationKey)\\n  .on<'payment.captured', { orderId: string }>(\\n    'payment.captured',\\n    (saga, event) => {\\n      saga.state.status = 'paid';\\n      return [send('inventory.reserve', { orderId: event.payload.orderId })];\\n    },\\n  )\\n  .on<'inventory.failed', Failure>('inventory.failed', (_saga, event) => [\\n    sagaCompensate(\\n      { type: 'payment.captured', payload: { orderId: event.payload.orderId } },\\n      event.payload.reason,\\n    ),\\n  ])\\n  .compensate<'payment.captured', { orderId: string }>(\\n    'payment.captured',\\n    (_saga, event) => [send('payment.refund', { orderId: event.payload.orderId })],\\n  )\\n  .build();\"\n  }\n] }) }}\n\n<p class=\"ns-lede\">\nThe definition correlates both events by <code>orderId</code>. When <code>inventory.failed</code>\narrives, its handler returns a compensation request for <code>payment.captured</code>. Executing that\nrequest needs a saga bus bridge with a compensator; surviving a restart needs a durable store. With\nthat wiring, the registered handler emits <code>payment.refund</code>.\n<a href=\"{{ '/durable-workflows/' |> url }}\">See the durability model</a>.\n</p>\n\n<nav class=\"ns-cluster\" aria-label=\"Choose the next page\">\n  <a href=\"{{ '/quickstart/' |> url }}\">Run it</a> ·\n  <a href=\"{{ '/concepts/' |> url }}\">Understand it</a> ·\n  <a href=\"{{ '/why/' |> url }}\">Decide whether it fits</a>\n</nav>\n","numLines":53,"startLine":1,"totalLines":53}}}
