{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_aeF1M5iGiINKnGxzmBwPOepP","type":"tool_result","content":"/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/index.vto:17:    body: \"Define state transitions and compensation in TypeScript; the runtime records every step through its saga store instead of treating a multi-step flow as a retry loop.\",\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/index.vto:36:    code: \"import { defineSaga, sagaCompensate, send } from '@netscript/plugin-sagas-core';\\nimport type { SagaCorrelationKey } from '@netscript/plugin-sagas-core';\\n\\ntype Checkout = { status: 'pending' | 'paid' };\\ntype Failure = { orderId: string; reason: string };\\ntype CheckoutEvent =\\n  | { type: 'payment.captured'; payload: { orderId: string } }\\n  | { type: 'inventory.failed'; payload: Failure };\\n\\nconst checkout = defineSaga('checkout')\\n  .state<Checkout>({ status: 'pending' })\\n  .correlate<CheckoutEvent>((event) => event.payload.orderId as SagaCorrelationKey)\\n  .on<'payment.captured', { orderId: string }>(\\n    'payment.captured',\\n    (saga, event) => {\\n      saga.state.status = 'paid';\\n      return [send('inventory.reserve', { orderId: event.payload.orderId })];\\n    },\\n  )\\n  .on<'inventory.failed', Failure>('inventory.failed', (_saga, event) => [\\n    sagaCompensate(\\n      { type: 'payment.captured', payload: { orderId: event.payload.orderId } },\\n      event.payload.reason,\\n    ),\\n  ])\\n  .compensate<'payment.captured', { orderId: string }>(\\n    'payment.captured',\\n    (_saga, event) => [send('payment.refund', { orderId: event.payload.orderId })],\\n  )\\n  .build();\"\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/index.vto:43:request needs a saga bus bridge with a compensator; surviving a restart needs a durable store. With\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/concepts.vto:47:“One plugin” is a packaging unit, not a runtime unit. Workers, sagas, triggers, and streams are the\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/why.vto:72:      desc: \"NetScript's saga core keeps TypeScript definitions, store and bus ports, transports, and compensation inside a broader application workspace. It is not a drop-in Temporal API.\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a83c9845-4a4d-49af-b9fe-4d6db86478d5","uuid":"11cc6453-8beb-44fb-a394-720441f83d45","timestamp":"2026-08-04T10:25:20.269Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/index.vto:17:    body: \"Define state transitions and compensation in TypeScript; the runtime records every step through its saga store instead of treating a multi-step flow as a retry loop.\",\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/index.vto:36:    code: \"import { defineSaga, sagaCompensate, send } from '@netscript/plugin-sagas-core';\\nimport type { SagaCorrelationKey } from '@netscript/plugin-sagas-core';\\n\\ntype Checkout = { status: 'pending' | 'paid' };\\ntype Failure = { orderId: string; reason: string };\\ntype CheckoutEvent =\\n  | { type: 'payment.captured'; payload: { orderId: string } }\\n  | { type: 'inventory.failed'; payload: Failure };\\n\\nconst checkout = defineSaga('checkout')\\n  .state<Checkout>({ status: 'pending' })\\n  .correlate<CheckoutEvent>((event) => event.payload.orderId as SagaCorrelationKey)\\n  .on<'payment.captured', { orderId: string }>(\\n    'payment.captured',\\n    (saga, event) => {\\n      saga.state.status = 'paid';\\n      return [send('inventory.reserve', { orderId: event.payload.orderId })];\\n    },\\n  )\\n  .on<'inventory.failed', Failure>('inventory.failed', (_saga, event) => [\\n    sagaCompensate(\\n      { type: 'payment.captured', payload: { orderId: event.payload.orderId } },\\n      event.payload.reason,\\n    ),\\n  ])\\n  .compensate<'payment.captured', { orderId: string }>(\\n    'payment.captured',\\n    (_saga, event) => [send('payment.refund', { orderId: event.payload.orderId })],\\n  )\\n  .build();\"\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/index.vto:43:request needs a saga bus bridge with a compensator; surviving a restart needs a durable store. With\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/concepts.vto:47:“One plugin” is a packaging unit, not a runtime unit. Workers, sagas, triggers, and streams are the\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/why.vto:72:      desc: \"NetScript's saga core keeps TypeScript definitions, store and bus ports, transports, and compensation inside a broader application workspace. It is not a drop-in Temporal API.\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
