{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_fa9012375f714b8ab4d31962","type":"tool_result","content":"/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/index.vto:27:    body: \"aspire start brings up the whole generated resource graph; the dashboard then reports resource health and carries logs and traces across it.\",\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/concepts.vto:16:{{ comp.diagram({ src: \"/assets/diagrams/architecture-overview.svg\", alt: \"A NetScript workspace: contracts define services; services and plugin runtimes connect to the Fresh web app; the AppHost materializes the resources and their infrastructure under one observed graph.\", caption: \"The mental model: contracts → services → plugins → web layer, with Aspire and telemetry connecting the running resources.\" }) }}\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/concepts.vto:33:resolve service URLs lazily from Aspire-injected environment values, so callers do not pin a\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/concepts.vto:44:those declarations into static workspace wiring, and Aspire can materialize a plugin's API and\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/concepts.vto:66:processes. The Aspire dashboard reads health, logs, traces, and metrics from that running graph;\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/concepts.vto:69:Aspire is the default local orchestration layer, not part of every package API. Without it, the Deno\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/concepts.vto:72:[Observability](/observability/), or [the Aspire boundary](/explanation/aspire/) for mechanics.\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/quickstart.vto:14:<strong><a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspire/\">.NET Aspire CLI</a></strong>, and start\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/quickstart.vto:39:cd my-app/aspire\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/quickstart.vto:40:aspire restore   # first run only\n/home/codex/repos/ns-mainpages/docs/site/quickstart.vto:41:aspire start\n/